<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Verbal Dictionary"/>
</example>
<example source="WE-ST008 3.2">
<form lang="kit"><text>Dibaya kälepalle danyroene, angde dowae mäse diga, ddia da dam dindugän a dägabällän. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I crept slowly towards it, and when I got close, the deer ran away and stood.</text></form>
</translation>
<note type="reference">
<form lang="kit"><text><span href="silfw://localhost/link?tool%3dinterlinearEdit%26guid%3d59ad9030-c509-42ae-829f-5d7ea6b83262%26tag%3d" class="Hyperlink">WE-ST008 3.2</span></text></form>
</note>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Verbal Dictionary"/>
</example>
<example source="WE-ST024 7.1">
<form lang="kit"><text>Oba ulle binang a dägabälleyo ada ddia bo sawe ttang alle a kottllam bo ttätt ttang alle.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Their big bosses stood like this: the deer's on the left hand side and the turtle's on the right hand side.</text></form>
</translation>
<note type="reference">
<form lang="kit"><text><span href="silfw://localhost/link?tool%3dinterlinearEdit%26guid%3db4d3aa8e-9355-4019-ac9c-789ce17851b3%26tag%3d" class="Hyperlink">WE-ST024 7.1</span></text></form>
</note>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Verbal Dictionary"/>
</example>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1.1 Stand"/>
<reversal type="en"><form lang="en"><text>stand</text></form>
</reversal>
