</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>banana_type</text></gloss>
<definition>
<form lang="en"><text>type of introduced banana</text></form>
<form lang="kit"><text>Tupi pänyanzag dan, obo däg a yuwog dag, ako käp a obo tutupi kanong dag. O me käp a obo otät ma da ako binzenen ma dag yu mi, a kire da yu ma dag. Ada pätt a obo tärpän ma dan popel e ankom peyang kaekep e. Pag peyang mer mokowang dan. (It grows big; its bunches are plentiful, and its fruit are a bit long. <span lang="en">When ripe, its fruit is eaten</span> and heated on the fire, and <span lang="en">when unripe, it's cooked.</span> The stem is cut for popel and chewed with ants. It's tasty with salt.)</text></form>
</definition>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Verbal Dictionary"/>
