<gloss lang="en"><text>banana_type</text></gloss>
<definition>
<form lang="en"><text>type of native banana</text></form>
<form lang="kit"><text>Tupi dan, obo käp a ulleulle dag, ge mabun up da. Obo käp a o me otät ma dan ako kire me yu ma dan. Da lla da ge up de botän suwe de mɨnyi sägäsägäd de bottän ako sägäsägäd de källa de bobewän. Ine da obo mamang abal dan ako tatu we mäkamäke ma dan itrellang att. (It's long, its fruits are big; this is a sacred banana.<span lang="en"> When ripe, its fruit is eaten, and when unripe, it's cooked.</span> If a person eats this banana, their urine and feces will be yellow. Its liquid is very red and it can be used to wash to avoid illness.)</text></form>
</definition>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Verbal Dictionary"/>
<example>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Verbal Dictionary"/>
</example>
