</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>ant</text></gloss>
<definition>
<form lang="en"><text>ant</text></form>
<form lang="kit"><text>Dälag dan. Obo ziz a kängkäm ma dan nane we kumye itrell täräp me. Ako mälläng obäd täräp me ziz a mälläng dungg ma dan llo ttam peyang länenatt me. Ziz de ada ma dan, be mägda da, bällkäp a wa miny a ddägnan ma dag. (<span lang="en">They are bitter. Insects are washed and drunk as medicine when you have a cough. Also, when you have a runny nose, you can smell them with crushed leaves. It's done this way with insects, but the mother and eggs are edible.)</span></text></form>
</definition>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Verbal Dictionary"/>
